---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Isaac Bright & Brighter Sites | Therapist Website Design"
  description="Meet Isaac Bright, the founder and builder behind Brighter Sites, and learn why Brighter Sites combines custom therapist website design with technical setup, SEO, analytics, and ongoing care."
>
  <section class="page-intro about-intro">
    <div class="container about-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About Brighter Sites</p>
        <h1>A website business that started with one counseling practice close to home.</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="about-lead">
        <p>
          Brighter Sites began when my wife decided to open her own counseling
          practice. I started researching what her website would need to do well,
          then built it from the ground up around the practice she was actually
          creating—not around a generic therapy template.
        </p>
        <p>
          That project made one thing very clear: a good practice website is much
          more than a collection of attractive pages.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section founder-section">
    <div class="container founder-grid">
      <aside class="founder-card" aria-label="Isaac Bright, founder of Brighter Sites">
        <p class="founder-card-label">Founder</p>
        <h2>Isaac Bright</h2>
        <p class="founder-role">Founder · Designer · Developer</p>
        <p class="founder-card-copy">
          Building thoughtful, effective websites for therapists and counseling
          practices—with the technical details handled carefully from the start.
        </p>

        <div class="founder-card-points" aria-label="Areas of focus">
          <span>Web design & development</span>
          <span>Security & performance</span>
          <span>Long-term website support</span>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="founder-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who you work with</p>
        <h2>I’m Isaac Bright, the person behind Brighter Sites.</h2>

        <p class="founder-lead">
          My background combines electronics and automation work with computer
          science, programming, and hands-on software development. I am currently
          completing a B.S. in Computer Science, with graduation expected
          November 11, 2026.
        </p>

        <p>
          The part of that background that matters most here is the way I approach
          problems. I like understanding how the whole system fits together,
          finding the part that is not working well, and building something that
          is practical to use and maintain afterward.
        </p>

        <p>
          That same approach carries into Brighter Sites. I am not interested in
          handing a practice a template and calling the job finished. I want to
          understand what the practice needs, build the site around it, handle the
          technical details carefully, and make sure there is a clear path for the
          site to keep improving after launch.
        </p>

        <div class="founder-principle">
          <strong>The goal is simple.</strong>
          <span>You should understand what you are paying for, who is doing the work, and what happens after the website launches.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container trust-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I handle</p>
        <h2>You are not just buying access to website software.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="responsibility-grid">
        <article>
          <span>Design & structure</span>
          <h3>A site built around the actual practice.</h3>
          <p>
            I work through the visual direction, page structure, mobile behavior,
            content organization, and client pathways instead of asking you to
            figure those decisions out inside a site builder.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>Technical setup</span>
          <h3>The pieces behind the website are part of the job.</h3>
          <p>
            Domains, DNS, launch configuration, search setup, analytics, mobile
            testing, and the other technical details are treated as part of a
            professional launch—not as problems you discover afterward.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>After launch</span>
          <h3>You can still have someone paying attention.</h3>
          <p>
            Ongoing care is optional, but it is available when you would rather
            have someone monitor the site, interpret the data, explain what it
            means, and make useful improvements over time.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-story">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why therapy practices</p>
        <h2>The website has a different job when someone is looking for help.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          A person visiting a counseling website may already feel uncertain,
          overwhelmed, or unsure whether a clinician is the right fit. The site
          needs to make important information easy to find without making the
          experience feel cold, cluttered, or unnecessarily complicated.
        </p>

        <p>
          It should help someone understand the practice, the services offered,
          the clinician or team, and what to do next. It should also represent
          the practice professionally enough that the person behind it feels
          comfortable sharing the website with a referral source, colleague, or
          prospective client.
        </p>

        <p>
          That combination of human presentation and technical discipline is the
          niche Brighter Sites is built around.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-standard-section">
    <div class="container standard-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How I want the business to work</p>
        <h2>No mystery around the web side of your practice.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="standard-list">
        <div>
          <strong>Explain the recommendation.</strong>
          <p>If I think something should change, you should understand why it matters.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Price work before it starts.</strong>
          <p>Defined additional work is quoted for approval instead of becoming an open-ended bill.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Separate your website from optional care.</strong>
          <p>You do not have to keep paying for ongoing management simply to keep the website you paid for.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Use data without pretending it is certainty.</strong>
          <p>Analytics and search data help us make better decisions; they are not an excuse for fake ranking guarantees.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The other half of the website</p>
        <h2>A beautiful site should also work hard behind the scenes.</h2>
        <p>
          Design is only the part people see first. Structure, mobile usability,
          performance, search visibility, analytics, and maintainability all
          affect how useful the site remains after launch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Thoughtful search structure</h3>
          <p>
            Clear service pages, useful page titles, understandable URLs, and a
            technically sound site structure help search engines understand what
            the practice offers and where it serves clients.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Useful measurement</h3>
          <p>
            Search and website data can show what is gaining attention, what is
            being overlooked, and where the next improvement may be worth making.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Cost-conscious growth</h3>
          <p>
            Good structure, useful content, performance, and organic search
            visibility can help a practice grow without depending entirely on
            paid advertising.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with a conversation</p>
        <h2>You do not need to know how the website should be built before you contact me.</h2>
        <p>
          Tell me about the practice, what you are trying to accomplish, and what
          you are unsure about. Part of my job is helping turn that into a clear
          website plan before you commit to the work.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Tell me about your practice</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero-grid,
  .founder-grid,
  .trust-split,
  .about-story,
  .standard-panel {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .about-intro h1 {
    max-width: 17ch;
  }

  .about-lead {
    align-self: end;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .about-lead p + p,
  .founder-copy > p + p,
  .about-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .founder-section {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .founder-card {
    align-self: start;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.7rem);
    border: 1px solid rgba(39,119,111,.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 14%, rgba(95,174,163,.24), transparent 24%),
      linear-gradient(145deg, #eef6f3, #f8f4ea 58%, #ffffff);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .founder-card-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: .35rem .65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--teal-dark);
    color: white;
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .founder-card h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .founder-role {
    margin-top: .35rem;
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-size: .84rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .founder-card-copy {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .founder-card-points {
    display: grid;
    gap: .65rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(39,119,111,.16);
  }

  .founder-card-points span {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: .82rem;
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .founder-card-points span::before {
    position: absolute;
    top: .48em;
    left: 0;
    width: .46rem;
    height: .46rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal);
    content: '';
  }

  .founder-copy h2,
  .trust-split h2,
  .about-story h2,
  .standard-panel h2 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .founder-copy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .founder-lead {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .founder-principle {
    display: grid;
    gap: .35rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
    background: var(--teal-light);
  }

  .founder-principle strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .founder-principle span {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .responsibility-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .responsibility-grid article {
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: white;
  }

  .responsibility-grid article > span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: .55rem;
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-size: .7rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .responsibility-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: .55rem;
  }

  .about-copy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .about-standard-section {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .standard-panel {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 90% 8%, rgba(95,174,163,.16), transparent 28%),
      #fffdf8;
  }

  .standard-list {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .standard-list > div {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .standard-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .standard-list p {
    margin-top: .3rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .about-hero-grid,
    .founder-grid,
    .trust-split,
    .about-story,
    .standard-panel {
      grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .founder-grid {
      grid-template-columns: .72fr 1.28fr;
    }
  }
</style>
